# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs
*.log

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.local

# Node (if added later)
node_modules/

# Generated design-review page — rebuild with tools/build-polish-preview.mjs.
# The *.json sources beside it ARE tracked: they are the offline colour cache
# tools/gen-tokens.mjs reads, so only this build output is ignored.
tools/.cache/polish-preview.html

# The same, for every other probe page written here. A probe is a fixture that renders
# one thing at one size so a colour or a geometry can be LOOKED at; it is not a page of
# the app, and a checked-in copy would be read as one. The generator that writes each —
# tools/.cache/*.mjs — is ignored with them, so nothing here outlives the question it
# was written for.
tools/.cache/*.html

# Screenshots tools/render-themes.mjs writes. They are EVIDENCE of a render, not
# an input to one: every shot is regenerated from the current source in a few
# seconds, and a checked-in PNG of a page that has since changed is worse than
# none, because it looks like the app.
tools/.cache/theme-shots/

# Throwaway driver scripts and their scratch output — a probe written to answer one
# question about one release, and the .txt files a shell command feeds it. Same
# reasoning as the shots above, one level up: they bake in a localhost URL and a
# hand-written fixture, so they are not a durable test and must not be read as one.
# The suites that DO belong to the repo are tools/smoke-*.mjs, which smoke-all.mjs
# globs. The *.json colour cache beside these stays tracked — tools/gen-tokens.mjs
# reads it.
tools/.cache/*.mjs
tools/.cache/*.js
tools/.cache/*.sh
tools/.cache/*.txt
tools/.cache/*.log

# The same two families again, which the list above was written without. A probe that
# answers a colour or geometry question in PowerShell is `tools/.cache/*.ps1` — the
# siblings of `make-icons.ps1` are real tools and stay tracked, so this cannot be
# `*.ps1` — and the contact sheets those probes draw land beside them as PNGs. Both are
# throwaway by the same argument as the shots above: they are EVIDENCE of one render, and
# a sheet left in the tree reads as a picture of the app. They were also, until now, the
# thing that blocked the deploy: tools/deploy-ghpages.mjs refuses on any
# `git status --porcelain` output, and a single untracked probe sheet produces exactly that.
tools/.cache/*.ps1
tools/.cache/*.png

# Build artifacts
dist/
# A third-party log analyser, downloaded to read for ideas. Not ours to commit.
indrones-dev-loganalyzer-*/

# The brand masters: four 2048px presentation plates plus the intro video, ~24 MB.
# What SHIPS is derived from them and IS tracked — assets/brand-panel-*.png and
# assets/brand-intro.mp4, produced by tools/make-brand-assets.ps1 — so a clone needs
# none of this. It also blocks every deploy while it sits untracked:
# tools/deploy-ghpages.mjs refuses on any `git status --porcelain` output.
Brand Elements I-PASSBOOK/
